 "text": "Hi, how are you today? Legal in some areas, annoying in others. Some areas ban camping altogether, and parking long than a few hours can get you to ticket. Pretty much, in some places. The alternative is a short hike in, which is fine for a night. Much quicker. And much safer. Parking near the tent is best in the morning. Then walk straight out through the gate in the evening. More like being in your own backyard. The big advantage is being able to leave little early, as in dark, and not worry about it.",
